  "hypothesis": "The missing Could not alloc rect message may be unreachable because the allocation wrapper never returns null.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Allocation failure stops in alloc or nhalloc before init_rect tests its result; successful initialization returns one full-map rectangle.",
  "observedBehavior": "Exact alloc/init_rect/free_rect bodies compiled in normal and MONITOR_HEAP configurations, with exact nhalloc in the latter. A deterministic malloc adapter returns null; a nonreturning panic capture verifies the allocator-level message is reached, never Could not alloc rect. Successful adapter controls exercise init/reinit/free/reinit and match production JS capacity56, count1 and full-map rectangle. global.h declares and documents the nonnull/nonreturning contract and monitor macro redirection.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "compiled_oracle",
    "scope": "Exact alloc/init_rect/free_rect bodies compiled in normal and MONITOR_HEAP configurations, with exact nhalloc in the latter. A deterministic malloc adapter returns null; a nonreturning panic capture verifies the allocator-level message is reached, never Could not alloc rect. Successful adapter controls exercise init/reinit/free/reinit and match production JS capacity56, count1 and full-map rectangle. global.h declares and documents the nonnull/nonreturning contract and monitor macro redirection.",
    "limitations": [
